          <msdyn_customconfiguration>{"version":"GptDynamicPrompt-2","prompt":[{"type":"literal","text":"You are tasked with extracting the most recent hearing date from an email chain. The hearing date may be explicitly stated as a calendar date or referenced using relative phrases such as \"today,\" \"tomorrow,\" or \"in 3 days.\" The goal is to identify the hearing date mentioned in the newest email of the chain if available; otherwise, consider older emails, prioritizing the most recent relevant date. The emails will most likely have dates in British dd/mm/yyyy format, so they should be interpreted in that way in the first instance.\n\n### Instructions:\n1. **Analyze the Email Chain:** Review the emails in chronological order, starting from the newest to the oldest.\n2. **Identify Hearing Dates:** Look for explicit dates or relative date phrases that likely indicate a hearing date, these are most likely in British date format dd/mm/yyyy\n3. **Resolve Relative Dates:** Convert relative date phrases into absolute dates based on the context or the date of the email in which they appear, use this date  "},{"type":"inputVariable","id":"Current_20Date"},{"type":"literal","text":"  if a timestamp is not available in the email.\n4. **Select the Most Recent Hearing Date:** Prefer hearing dates found in newer emails over older ones, if multiple dates are found, use the closest to today that is either today or in the future\n5. **Output the Result:** Return the hearing date as a JSON object with the property \"hearingDate\" formatted in ISO 8601 (YYYY-MM-DD). If no hearing date is found, return null for the property.\n6. Output the reason why a date was chosen or not found as a JSON property called \"reason\".\n\n### Output Format:\n```json\n{\n  \"hearingDate\": \"{ISO 8601 date string or null}\",\n  \"reason\": \"the reason the hearing date was chosen or not found\"\n}\n```\n\n### Guidelines:\n- Extract dates only from the provided email chain.\n- Interpret relative date phrases accurately based on the email's timestamp or use this date  "},{"type":"inputVariable","id":"Current_20Date"},{"type":"literal","text":" if the email timestamp is not available\n- If multiple hearing dates are found, choose the one from the newest email.\n- Return null if no hearing date is identified.\n\nProvide the email chain here:  "},{"type":"inputVariable","id":"Email_20Chain"},{"type":"literal","text":" \nProvide the current date:  "},{"type":"inputVariable","id":"Current_20Date"},{"type":"literal","text":" \n"}],"definitions":{"inputs":[{"id":"Email_20Chain","text":"Email Chain","type":"text","quickTestValue":"My hearing is on 23/3/26 at Norwich and I have a question about that.\nChris Way\nDevelopment Team Manager\nLow Code Platform Team | Digital and Technology Services | HMCTS\ngov.uk/hmcts\n"},{"id":"Current_20Date","text":"Current Date","type":"text","quickTestValue":"20/03/2026"}],"formulas":[],"data":[],"output":{"formats":["json"],"jsonSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"hearingDate":{"type":"string"},"reason":{"type":"string"}}},"jsonExamples":[{"hearingDate":"2026-03-23","reason":"The newest email explicitly states the hearing date as 23/3/26, which is interpreted as 23 March 2026 in British date format."}]}},"modelParameters":{"modelType":"gpt-41-mini","gptParameters":{"temperature":0}},"settings":{"recordRetrievalLimit":30,"shouldPreserveRecordLinks":null,"runtime":null},"code":""}</msdyn_customconfiguration>
